# Search input

A labelled search field helps people find a specific item when browsing is not enough.

These are civica reference implementations for component authors. They do not replace native Home Assistant behaviour or demonstrate a connection to a live home.

## Search field, filters or finder

This page owns the labelled query input. A complete search needs more than the field:

| Layer | Responsibility | Owner |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Query input | Visible label, named scope, keyboard submission and retained query | This page |
| Suggestions | Optional help entering a known query; free text still works | [Native datalist reference](../publishing/components/search-autocomplete.html) |
| Query and filters | Apply, clear, result counts, no matches and query/facet combination | [Search-filter pattern](../publishing/patterns/search-filter.html) |
| Collection page | Result descriptions, permitted dataset, destinations and context | [Finder composition](../publishing/frontend-templates/finder.html) |

The examples demonstrate fixed records or local feedback, as each description states. They do not implement a native entity or target picker. Keep Home Assistant’s picker when selection must respect capability, permission, domain or action-target rules.

## When to use it

Use it for a long device list or a help index. State what is being searched so results are predictable. Search can complement filters and sorting.

## When not to use it

Do not make search compensate for missing room navigation. Do not silently combine devices, automations and external web results without explaining the scope.

## Home Assistant adaptation

Preserve the current query when returning from a result. Distinguish no matching devices from a failed connection, and keep a clear route to the unfiltered list. Search in a reference frame changes no Home Assistant state; its feedback describes only the demonstration.

## Accessibility and behaviour

Use a search landmark with a unique label when several searches exist. Provide a visible input label and a text button. A browser-supplied clear icon is an enhancement, not the only way to reset the query.

